WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.520
So it's still very, very early.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:07.069
And we want to be really careful not to overstate
the promise or the potential of any one treatment

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:08.440
for coronavirus.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.910
But I did want to update you about chloroquine.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:17.239
We have news that the FDA has approved on
an emergency use basis the use of chloroquine

00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:23.840
and hydroxy chloroquine from the strategic
national stockpile to look at using it to

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.600
treat corona virus in some patients.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.930
Now, I want to be really clear here, because
there's so many people misunderstanding this

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.300
because Donald Trump has been overselling
it.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.290
There are many possible treatments being looked
at.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.480
OK, we've got chloroquine with and without
a throw myson.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.320
We've got Ramdas Vier.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:47.020
We have a combination of two different HIV
drugs with and without a zero myson.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.540
We've got some antibody treatments, convalescent
plasma or plasma, as Donald Trump referred

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.900
to it a few days ago, dozens of other possibilities,
drugs in development.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.040
There's there's dozens and dozens of things
going on.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.560
Trump has been overselling chloroquine with
a zero myson for a couple of weeks now.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.181
Dr. Anthony Foushee has been careful not to
oversell it.

00:01:09.181 --> 00:01:11.110
It is not a proven treatment.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:17.960
The letter that we now have seen from the
FDA, which does approve this for some emergency

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:24.011
use, is also very cautious to say that this
is not a drug approved for treating Corona

00:01:24.011 --> 00:01:25.011
virus.

00:01:25.011 --> 00:01:30.729
The FDA goes on to say, based upon limited
in vitro and anecdotal clinical data in case

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:36.659
series chloroquine and chloroquine hydroxy
chloroquine sulfate are currently recommended

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:40.830
for treatment of hospitalized coronavirus
patients in several countries.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:45.060
And a number of national guidelines report
incorporating recommendations regarding use

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.540
of it in the setting of Cauvin 19.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:54.479
The FDA encourages the conduct and participation
in randomized controlled clinical trials that

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:58.680
may produce evidence concerning the effectiveness
in treating coronavirus.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:05.850
The FDA is issuing an emergency use emergency
use number what a stands for.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:12.159
But the idea of allowing emergency use to
facilitate the availability of chloroquine

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:18.109
during the pandemic to treat patients for
whom a clinical trial is not available or

00:02:18.109 --> 00:02:19.529
participation is not feasible.

00:02:19.529 --> 00:02:23.689
So making clear that we're not approving the
drug for chloroquine, we're approving the

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:29.180
drug for discretionary emergency use when
the patient can't participate in a clinical

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.180
trial.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:35.519
It goes on to say, having concluded that the
criteria for issuance of this authorization

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:36.599
is met.

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:42.549
I am authorizing the emergency use as described
in the scope of authorization for treatment

00:02:42.549 --> 00:02:48.489
of coronavirus when clinical trials are not
available or participation is not feasible.

00:02:48.489 --> 00:02:53.709
So we are waiting on results from what are
called randomized clinical randomized controlled

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:54.969
trials.

00:02:54.969 --> 00:03:01.389
What we have so far as a number of small trials
have shown is conflicting information.

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:07.969
We have some small sample sizes that say the
chloroquine treatment has worked well.

00:03:07.969 --> 00:03:12.480
We have other small samples that say, you
know, the people who didn't get it did just

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.090
as well as the people who did.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:20.219
And as Anthony Foushee has pointed out, you
have to be comparing the new treatment to

00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:25.670
some standard of care and you need to be randomizing
it.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:31.219
Just because we've found some small studies
with a core correlation does not mean that

00:03:31.219 --> 00:03:34.400
we have found a causal link and case in point.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.269
When you see just as many studies that say
the control group did just as well, you have

00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:42.170
to question the value of this as a therapeutic
treatment.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:47.860
We need a large, properly done, randomized
controlled trial.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.489
Until we get that, we won't really know.

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:52.200
So the FDA, I believe, is doing the right
thing here.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.680
It seems that the side effects and the risks
are reasonable, assuming that you're getting

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.060
an EKG of patients that you're going to give
this treatment to.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:05.670
Chloroquine can affect what's called the Kutty
UTC interval to heart related thing.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:11.409
The FDA says in limited situations it can
be tried when you can't get access to a clinical

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:12.409
trial.

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:14.709
Doing the EKG is a very important thing.

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:17.150
It's a constant balance of risk.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.090
Reward side effects and the impact of not
trying it.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.770
When things start to get very, very dire.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:30.810
Meanwhile, there are also people who are taking
chloroquine for the actual approved uses who

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:36.290
are now having trouble getting it because
many countries are starting to stockpile chloroquine.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.290
That's another issue which we'll talk about
at another time.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.350
But everything has a cost is the point.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.440
Let's take a quick break.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:43.912
Much more coming up right after this.

